{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"urn:solid:Agent","@type":"rdfs:Class","rdfs:label":"Agent","rdfs:comment":"A thing that acts — person, organization, group, or software.","owl:sameAs":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent","rdfs:seeAlso":["http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent","https://www.w3.org/ns/activitystreams#Object"],"notToBeConfusedWith":["urn:solid:Person"],"status":"stable","added":"2026-04-18","notes":"Use when the actor could be non-human (a bot, a group, a service). Prefer `urn:solid:Person` when you know the actor is specifically a human.","examples":[{"title":"Software agent","jsonld":{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"https://example.org/bots/curator","@type":"urn:solid:Agent","foaf:name":"Curator Bot"}}],"provenance":{"sources":["http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent"],"curatedBy":"bootstrap"},"history":[{"event":"added","at":"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z","by":"bootstrap","note":"Initial term."}],"see_also":{"corpus":"/corpus.jsonl","schema":"/schema/term.schema.json","index":"/index.json","llms":"/llms.txt"}}
{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"urn:solid:Group","@type":"rdfs:Class","rdfs:label":"Group","rdfs:comment":"A collection of agents — informal or ad-hoc, not necessarily a formal organization.","owl:sameAs":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Group","rdfs:seeAlso":["http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#Group","https://www.w3.org/ns/activitystreams#Group"],"notToBeConfusedWith":["urn:solid:Organization"],"status":"stable","added":"2026-04-18","notes":"Subclass of `urn:solid:Agent`. Use for any collection of agents — friends, mailing-list subscribers, project contributors. Use `urn:solid:Organization` when the collective has formal/legal structure. Members are listed with `urn:solid:member`.","examples":[{"title":"A simple Group","jsonld":{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"https://example.org/groups/admins","@type":"urn:solid:Group","urn:solid:name":"Admins","urn:solid:member":[{"@id":"https://example.org/alice#me"},{"@id":"https://example.org/bob#me"}]}}],"provenance":{"sources":["http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Group"],"curatedBy":"claude-curate-next"},"history":[{"event":"added","at":"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z","by":"claude-curate-next","note":"Initial term."}],"see_also":{"corpus":"/corpus.jsonl","schema":"/schema/term.schema.json","index":"/index.json","llms":"/llms.txt"}}
{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"urn:solid:OnlineAccount","@type":"rdfs:Class","rdfs:label":"OnlineAccount","rdfs:comment":"An account held by an Agent on some online service.","owl:sameAs":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/OnlineAccount","rdfs:seeAlso":["http://www.w3.org/ns/solid/terms#Account"],"status":"stable","added":"2026-04-18","notes":"Use as the value type of `urn:solid:account`. Typically described with `foaf:accountName` (the username) and `foaf:accountServiceHomepage` (the service's homepage). For a Solid pod account specifically, see `solid:Account`.","examples":[{"title":"An OnlineAccount on a service","jsonld":{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"https://example.org/alice/accounts/github","@type":"urn:solid:OnlineAccount","http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/accountName":"alice","http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/accountServiceHomepage":{"@id":"https://github.com/"}}}],"provenance":{"sources":["http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/OnlineAccount"],"curatedBy":"claude-curate-next"},"history":[{"event":"added","at":"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z","by":"claude-curate-next","note":"Initial term."}],"see_also":{"corpus":"/corpus.jsonl","schema":"/schema/term.schema.json","index":"/index.json","llms":"/llms.txt"}}
{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"urn:solid:Organization","@type":"rdfs:Class","rdfs:label":"Organization","rdfs:comment":"A formal organization — a company, society, institution, or other collective with structure.","owl:sameAs":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Organization","rdfs:seeAlso":["https://schema.org/Organization","http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#Organization","http://www.w3.org/ns/org#Organization"],"notToBeConfusedWith":["urn:solid:Agent"],"status":"stable","added":"2026-04-18","notes":"Subclass of `urn:solid:Agent`: every Organization is an Agent, but not every Agent is an Organization (people, software). Use `Organization` when the actor has formal/legal structure; use `Agent` when the actor's nature is unspecified or could be a person.","examples":[{"title":"A simple organization","jsonld":{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"https://example.org/acme","@type":"urn:solid:Organization","urn:solid:name":"Acme Corp","urn:solid:homepage":{"@id":"https://acme.example.org/"}}}],"provenance":{"sources":["http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Organization"],"curatedBy":"claude-curate-next"},"history":[{"event":"added","at":"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z","by":"claude-curate-next","note":"Initial term."}],"see_also":{"corpus":"/corpus.jsonl","schema":"/schema/term.schema.json","index":"/index.json","llms":"/llms.txt"}}
{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"urn:solid:Person","@type":"rdfs:Class","rdfs:label":"Person","rdfs:comment":"A human being.","owl:sameAs":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Person","rdfs:seeAlso":["https://schema.org/Person","http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#Individual"],"notToBeConfusedWith":["urn:solid:Agent"],"status":"stable","added":"2026-04-18","notes":"Use for any human individual. Prefer this over `vcard:Individual` unless vCard-specific properties are needed, and over `schema:Person` when interoperating with FOAF-based Solid data.","examples":[{"title":"Minimal JSON-LD","jsonld":{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"https://example.org/alice#me","@type":"urn:solid:Person","foaf:name":"Alice"}}],"provenance":{"sources":["http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Person","https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-solid/"],"curatedBy":"bootstrap"},"history":[{"event":"added","at":"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z","by":"bootstrap","note":"Initial term."}],"see_also":{"corpus":"/corpus.jsonl","schema":"/schema/term.schema.json","index":"/index.json","llms":"/llms.txt"}}
{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"urn:solid:account","@type":"rdf:Property","rdfs:label":"account","rdfs:comment":"An online account held by the subject.","owl:sameAs":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/account","rdfs:seeAlso":["http://www.w3.org/ns/solid/terms#account"],"rdfs:domain":"urn:solid:Agent","rdfs:range":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/OnlineAccount","status":"stable","added":"2026-04-18","notes":"The value is an `OnlineAccount` resource describing the account (the service it lives on, the account name, etc.), not the bare account URL. For a Solid pod-specific notion of account ownership, see `solid:account`.","examples":[{"title":"Person with a GitHub account","jsonld":{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"https://example.org/alice#me","@type":"urn:solid:Person","urn:solid:account":{"@type":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/OnlineAccount","http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/accountName":"alice","http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/accountServiceHomepage":{"@id":"https://github.com/"}}}}],"provenance":{"sources":["http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/account"],"curatedBy":"claude-curate-next"},"history":[{"event":"added","at":"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z","by":"claude-curate-next","note":"Initial term."}],"see_also":{"corpus":"/corpus.jsonl","schema":"/schema/term.schema.json","index":"/index.json","llms":"/llms.txt"}}
{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"urn:solid:depiction","@type":"rdf:Property","rdfs:label":"depiction","rdfs:comment":"An image that depicts the subject.","owl:sameAs":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/depiction","rdfs:seeAlso":["https://schema.org/image","http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#hasPhoto"],"rdfs:range":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Image","status":"stable","added":"2026-04-18","notes":"The value is the IRI of the image itself, not a document containing it. Inverse of `foaf:depicts`. For a profile photo specifically, `vcard:hasPhoto` is often more appropriate in vCard-flavored data.","examples":[{"title":"Person with an avatar","jsonld":{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"https://example.org/alice#me","@type":"urn:solid:Person","urn:solid:depiction":{"@id":"https://example.org/alice/avatar.jpg"}}}],"provenance":{"sources":["http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/depiction"],"curatedBy":"claude-curate-next"},"history":[{"event":"added","at":"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z","by":"claude-curate-next","note":"Initial term."}],"see_also":{"corpus":"/corpus.jsonl","schema":"/schema/term.schema.json","index":"/index.json","llms":"/llms.txt"}}
{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"urn:solid:homepage","@type":"rdf:Property","rdfs:label":"homepage","rdfs:comment":"A homepage for the subject — a top-level page about the agent.","owl:sameAs":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/homepage","rdfs:seeAlso":["http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#hasURL","https://schema.org/url"],"rdfs:domain":"urn:solid:Agent","status":"stable","added":"2026-04-18","notes":"Inverse-functional in FOAF: a homepage uniquely identifies its agent. Use the IRI of the actual page, not a description of it. For arbitrary URLs that are not the canonical homepage, prefer `schema:url` or `vcard:hasURL`.","examples":[{"title":"Person with a homepage","jsonld":{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"https://example.org/alice#me","@type":"urn:solid:Person","urn:solid:homepage":{"@id":"https://alice.example.org/"}}}],"provenance":{"sources":["http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/homepage"],"curatedBy":"claude-curate-next"},"history":[{"event":"added","at":"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z","by":"claude-curate-next","note":"Initial term."}],"see_also":{"corpus":"/corpus.jsonl","schema":"/schema/term.schema.json","index":"/index.json","llms":"/llms.txt"}}
{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"urn:solid:img","@type":"rdf:Property","rdfs:label":"img","rdfs:comment":"An image that represents the person — typically a headshot or portrait.","owl:sameAs":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/img","rdfs:seeAlso":["urn:solid:depiction","http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#hasPhoto","https://schema.org/image"],"rdfs:domain":"urn:solid:Person","rdfs:range":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Image","notToBeConfusedWith":["urn:solid:depiction"],"status":"stable","added":"2026-04-18","notes":"A sub-property of `foaf:depiction` specifically for a portrait of a person. Prefer `urn:solid:depiction` when the subject is any kind of thing or the image is not a portrait. A person may have at most one primary `img` but multiple `depiction` values.","examples":[{"title":"Person with a portrait","jsonld":{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"https://example.org/alice#me","@type":"urn:solid:Person","urn:solid:img":{"@id":"https://example.org/alice/portrait.jpg"}}}],"provenance":{"sources":["http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/img"],"curatedBy":"claude-curate-next"},"history":[{"event":"added","at":"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z","by":"claude-curate-next","note":"Initial term."}],"see_also":{"corpus":"/corpus.jsonl","schema":"/schema/term.schema.json","index":"/index.json","llms":"/llms.txt"}}
{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"urn:solid:jabberID","@type":"rdf:Property","rdfs:label":"jabberID","rdfs:comment":"A Jabber/XMPP identifier for the Agent.","owl:sameAs":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/jabberID","rdfs:seeAlso":["http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#hasInstantMessage"],"rdfs:domain":"urn:solid:Agent","rdfs:range":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string","status":"stable","added":"2026-04-18","notes":"Inverse-functional in FOAF — a Jabber ID uniquely identifies its owner. The value is a bare JID string like `alice@jabber.example.org`, not a `xmpp:` URI. For other instant-messaging handles, see `vcard:hasInstantMessage`.","examples":[{"title":"Person with a Jabber ID","jsonld":{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"https://example.org/alice#me","@type":"urn:solid:Person","urn:solid:jabberID":"alice@jabber.example.org"}}],"provenance":{"sources":["http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/jabberID"],"curatedBy":"claude-curate-next"},"history":[{"event":"added","at":"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z","by":"claude-curate-next","note":"Initial term."}],"see_also":{"corpus":"/corpus.jsonl","schema":"/schema/term.schema.json","index":"/index.json","llms":"/llms.txt"}}
{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"urn:solid:knows","@type":"rdf:Property","rdfs:label":"knows","rdfs:comment":"A person known by the subject — a directed acquaintance relationship.","owl:sameAs":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/knows","rdfs:seeAlso":["https://schema.org/knows"],"rdfs:domain":"urn:solid:Person","rdfs:range":"urn:solid:Person","status":"stable","added":"2026-04-18","notes":"Asymmetric by default: A knows B does not imply B knows A. Use repeatedly to enumerate the social graph. The FOAF tradition treats this loosely — any acknowledged acquaintance counts.","examples":[{"title":"Alice knows Bob","jsonld":{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"https://example.org/alice#me","@type":"urn:solid:Person","urn:solid:knows":{"@id":"https://example.org/bob#me"}}}],"provenance":{"sources":["http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/knows"],"curatedBy":"claude-curate-next"},"history":[{"event":"added","at":"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z","by":"claude-curate-next","note":"Initial term."}],"see_also":{"corpus":"/corpus.jsonl","schema":"/schema/term.schema.json","index":"/index.json","llms":"/llms.txt"}}
{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"urn:solid:mbox","@type":"rdf:Property","rdfs:label":"mbox","rdfs:comment":"A personal mailbox — typically a mailto: IRI.","owl:sameAs":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/mbox","rdfs:seeAlso":["https://schema.org/email","http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#hasEmail"],"rdfs:domain":"urn:solid:Agent","status":"stable","added":"2026-04-18","notes":"Inverse-functional in FOAF: an mbox value uniquely identifies its owner, so two agents with the same mbox are the same agent. Prefer a `mailto:` IRI as the value, not a bare string. For a plain string email, see `vcard:hasEmail` or `schema:email`.","examples":[{"title":"Person with mailbox","jsonld":{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"https://example.org/alice#me","@type":"urn:solid:Person","urn:solid:mbox":{"@id":"mailto:alice@example.org"}}}],"provenance":{"sources":["http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/mbox"],"curatedBy":"claude-curate-next"},"history":[{"event":"added","at":"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z","by":"claude-curate-next","note":"Initial term."}],"see_also":{"corpus":"/corpus.jsonl","schema":"/schema/term.schema.json","index":"/index.json","llms":"/llms.txt"}}
{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"urn:solid:member","@type":"rdf:Property","rdfs:label":"member","rdfs:comment":"An agent that is a member of the group.","owl:sameAs":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/member","rdfs:seeAlso":["https://schema.org/member","http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#hasMember"],"rdfs:domain":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Group","rdfs:range":"urn:solid:Agent","status":"stable","added":"2026-04-18","notes":"Use to enumerate the agents that belong to a group. Repeated to list multiple members. The subject should typically be a `foaf:Group`; the value can be any Agent (Person, Organization, Group, software).","examples":[{"title":"Group with two members","jsonld":{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"https://example.org/groups/admins","@type":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Group","urn:solid:member":[{"@id":"https://example.org/alice#me"},{"@id":"https://example.org/bob#me"}]}}],"provenance":{"sources":["http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/member"],"curatedBy":"claude-curate-next"},"history":[{"event":"added","at":"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z","by":"claude-curate-next","note":"Initial term."}],"see_also":{"corpus":"/corpus.jsonl","schema":"/schema/term.schema.json","index":"/index.json","llms":"/llms.txt"}}
{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"urn:solid:name","@type":"rdf:Property","rdfs:label":"name","rdfs:comment":"A name for the subject.","owl:sameAs":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name","rdfs:seeAlso":["https://schema.org/name","http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#fn","http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"],"rdfs:domain":"urn:solid:Agent","rdfs:range":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string","status":"stable","added":"2026-04-18","notes":"The canonical display name. For structured names (given/family), use `foaf:givenName` and `foaf:familyName` directly until urn-solid ships equivalents.","examples":[{"title":"On a Person","jsonld":{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"https://example.org/alice#me","@type":"urn:solid:Person","urn:solid:name":"Alice"}}],"provenance":{"sources":["http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name"],"curatedBy":"bootstrap"},"history":[{"event":"added","at":"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z","by":"bootstrap","note":"Initial term."}],"see_also":{"corpus":"/corpus.jsonl","schema":"/schema/term.schema.json","index":"/index.json","llms":"/llms.txt"}}
{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"urn:solid:nick","@type":"rdf:Property","rdfs:label":"nick","rdfs:comment":"A short informal nickname for the subject — typically a chat handle or screen name.","owl:sameAs":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/nick","rdfs:seeAlso":["http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#hasNickname","https://schema.org/alternateName"],"rdfs:range":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string","notToBeConfusedWith":["urn:solid:name"],"status":"stable","added":"2026-04-18","notes":"For informal handles (IRC, IM, screen names) rather than legal or display names. A subject may have many nicknames across different contexts. Use `urn:solid:name` for the canonical display name.","examples":[{"title":"Person with a chat nick","jsonld":{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"https://example.org/alice#me","@type":"urn:solid:Person","urn:solid:nick":"ali"}}],"provenance":{"sources":["http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/nick"],"curatedBy":"claude-curate-next"},"history":[{"event":"added","at":"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z","by":"claude-curate-next","note":"Initial term."}],"see_also":{"corpus":"/corpus.jsonl","schema":"/schema/term.schema.json","index":"/index.json","llms":"/llms.txt"}}
{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"urn:solid:openid","@type":"rdf:Property","rdfs:label":"openid","rdfs:comment":"An OpenID identifier for the Agent — a document used to verify the Agent's identity.","owl:sameAs":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/openid","rdfs:seeAlso":["http://www.w3.org/ns/solid/terms#oidcIssuer"],"rdfs:domain":"urn:solid:Agent","rdfs:range":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document","status":"stable","added":"2026-04-18","notes":"Inverse-functional in FOAF — an OpenID document uniquely identifies its Agent. Predates Solid OIDC; for modern Solid pods use `solid:oidcIssuer` instead, which points at the OpenID Connect issuer URL.","examples":[{"title":"Person with an OpenID document","jsonld":{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"https://example.org/alice#me","@type":"urn:solid:Person","urn:solid:openid":{"@id":"https://alice.example.org/openid"}}}],"provenance":{"sources":["http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/openid"],"curatedBy":"claude-curate-next"},"history":[{"event":"added","at":"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z","by":"claude-curate-next","note":"Initial term."}],"see_also":{"corpus":"/corpus.jsonl","schema":"/schema/term.schema.json","index":"/index.json","llms":"/llms.txt"}}
{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"urn:solid:weblog","@type":"rdf:Property","rdfs:label":"weblog","rdfs:comment":"A weblog (blog) of the subject — the document the agent publishes posts to.","owl:sameAs":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/weblog","rdfs:seeAlso":["https://schema.org/blogPost","urn:solid:homepage"],"rdfs:domain":"urn:solid:Agent","rdfs:range":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document","notToBeConfusedWith":["urn:solid:homepage"],"status":"stable","added":"2026-04-18","notes":"Points at the blog as a whole, not at an individual post. An agent may have multiple weblogs (personal, work, project-specific). Use `urn:solid:homepage` for the main page about the agent rather than their writing feed.","examples":[{"title":"Person with a weblog","jsonld":{"@context":"https://urn-solid.github.io/context.jsonld","@id":"https://example.org/alice#me","@type":"urn:solid:Person","urn:solid:weblog":{"@id":"https://alice.example.org/blog/"}}}],"provenance":{"sources":["http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/weblog"],"curatedBy":"claude-curate-next"},"history":[{"event":"added","at":"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z","by":"claude-curate-next","note":"Initial term."}],"see_also":{"corpus":"/corpus.jsonl","schema":"/schema/term.schema.json","index":"/index.json","llms":"/llms.txt"}}
